  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "The best configuration so far is config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted; acc=0.725). The dominant signal is clearly RNA (rna_only multiprofile=0.653 vs image_only≈0.227), yet we have only tested scvi_n200 and pca_n2000 as RNA encoders; scgpt remains untested. Config_034 changes exactly one variable from the best config (RNA encoder: scvi_n200→scgpt) while holding the multiprofile + transformer + weighted + imagenet_vit_l regime fixed. This isolates the effect of RNA representation quality in the highest-performing setting. If scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it broadens our design space; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 is the right encoder and redirects budget toward image-encoder or fusion variations. Under a limited budget, testing the most impactful untested component (RNA encoder) in the proven best regime is the highest-information single experiment."
}

